| Metric | Value |
|---|---|
| **Total Findings** | 1 |
| **Critical** | 1 |
| **High** | 0 |
| **Medium** | 0 |
| **Low** | 0 |
| **Overall Score** | **5 / 100** |
| **Verdict** | **FAIL** |

The single finding is high-confidence and directly evidenced by the code. Using MD5 for password hashing is one of the most well-established credential-handling anti-patterns and represents a critical vulnerability in any system that stores or verifies user passwords.
