### PERF-003: No Error Isolation — Single Failure Rejects Entire Batch
**Severity**: High
**Location**: Lines 4–10 — the `Promise.all(...)` block

**Description**: `Promise.all` rejects immediately when any single promise rejects. If `JSON.parse` throws on one malformed message (line 6), or any of the three async calls fails for one message, the entire batch of up to 100 messages is abandoned. Messages that were in-flight but not yet acknowledged are neither acked nor nacked, leaving them invisible in the queue until the visibility timeout expires. Messages that completed successfully before the rejection still get their ack, but messages that hadn't started yet are silently dropped for this iteration.

**Impact**: Under real-world conditions where even a small fraction of messages are malformed or cause transient errors, this pattern causes repeated reprocessing of the entire batch (visibility timeout re-delivery), increased latency for all messages in the batch, and potential duplicate processing of already-acked messages if retried.

**Recommendation**: Use `Promise.allSettled` and handle failures individually:

```typescript
const results = await Promise.allSettled(messages.map(async (msg) => {
  const data = JSON.parse(msg.body);
  await processRecord(data);
  await enrichFromExternalAPI(data);
  await saveToDatabase(data);
  await queue.ack(msg);
}));

for (const result of results) {
  if (result.status === 'rejected') {
    // log error, nack message, send to DLQ, etc.
  }
}
```

